    "content": "NASA (National Aeronautics and Space Administration) owns and leads the Artemis II mission. While NASA owns the mission and the capsule, major aerospace contractors built the hardware: Lockheed Martin (LMT) built the Orion capsule, Boeing (BA) built the Space Launch System (SLS) rocket core, and Northrop Grumman (NOC) produced the boosters. Key facts about Artemis II ownership and construction: Mission Owner: NASA, specifically the Exploration Ground Systems team based at Kennedy Space Center. Orion Spacecraft: Built by Lockheed Martin (prime contractor), with modules and systems developed by contractors including Airbus. Lockheed Martin Launch System (SLS): Developed by Boeing (core stage) and Northrop Grumman (solid rocket boosters). Boeing Northrop Grumman Handover: Lockheed Martin officially handed over the finished Orion capsule to NASA on May 1, 2025, for final launch processing. Commercial Partnerships: While Artemis II is a NASA-owned mission, it incorporates components from commercial partners such as SpaceX and Blue Origin to support the broader, long-term Artemis program. SpaceX Blue Origin This video shows the Orion spacecraft's journey to the moon:1mVideoFromSpaceYouTube• Mar 31, 2026 1m The mission is scheduled for a crewed fly-around of the Moon in 2026, featuring astronauts from NASA and the Canadian Space Agency.",
